# sha256 manifest for the workload blobs of hca_compress_c128_h512_r64.
#
# The blobs are ~271 MB and are not committed; data/ is gitignored. They are a
# deterministic function of four pinned inputs, so they are rebuilt rather than
# stored, and this file is what makes "rebuilt" checkable:
#
#   corpus            tools/corpus/hca_v1.txt
#                     sha256 3e3b3cf574217c6921adee3189981483d3e7fe599afea42262318cdf43a46b8f
#   DeepSeek-V2-Lite  deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite
#                     revision 604d5664dddd88a0433dbae533b7fe9472482de0
#   DeepSeek-V4-Flash deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash
#                     revision 60d8d70770c6776ff598c94bb586a859a38244f1
#   per-workload seed workload_seed(uuid) = 0x11CA ^ crc32(uuid)
#                     (tools/gen_workload_blobs.py)
#
# Rebuild and verify:
#
#   python tools/gen_workload_blobs.py --root <root>
#   cd <root> && sha256sum -c $REPO/tasks/hca_compress_c128/blobs.sha256
#
# Paths are relative to the TraceSet root, matching the `path` field of each
# SafetensorsInput in hca_compress_c128_h512_r64.jsonl. Nothing upstream checks
# this: SafetensorsInput carries only (type, path, tensor_key) with no digest,
# and a Trace names its definition and solution by name alone -- so a blob that
# silently changed would re-score under the old trace's identity with no
# complaint anywhere. This file is that missing check.
#
# A mismatch means the blobs no longer match the recorded traces. Re-run
# tools/run_benchmark.py; do not edit this file to agree with the new blobs
# unless you meant to change them.
#
# Entry count tracks the workload jsonl exactly: one blob per workload, 23 of
# them as of the num_compressed 2048/4096/8192 points. Adding a sweep point to
# tools/build_hca_task.py therefore makes this file short by one and
# tools/stage_trace_set.py::_verify_blobs fails the stage with "referenced by a
# workload but absent from blobs.sha256" until it is regenerated. That is the
# intended failure mode -- it is the only thing that catches a half-updated
# sweep -- so regenerate rather than hand-appending.

